## DBsubject(Mechanics)
## DBchapter(Oscillatory Motion and Waves)
## DBsection(The Simple Pendulum)
## Date(December 2017)
## Institution(Brock University)
## Author(Brandon Lostracco)
## Edited (Connor Wilson, May 1, 2018)
## TitleText1('College Physics')
## AuthorText1('Urone et. al')
## EditionText1('2017')
## Section1('16.4')
## Problem1('5')
## KEYWORDS(frequency, period, harmonic, Hooke's)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$mass   = random(5.00, 10.00, 1.03);
$length = random(0.02, 0.06,  0.001);

$A1 = 1 / Compute("2pi*sqrt($length/9.8)");

BEGIN_PGML
The pendulum on a cuckoo clock is [`[$length]`] [`\textrm{m}`] long. What is its frequency?

[_]{$A1}  [`\textrm{Hz}`]

END_PGML
BEGIN_PGML_HINT
Recall the formula giving the frequency of a simple pendulum as a function of its length.
END_PGML_HINT

ENDDOCUMENT();
